title: Rotate in the Scene view
intro: Drag the round handle above the selection to turn it, right in the Scene view.
project: TopDown | Scene Rotate

create: Sprite
rename: Post
set: Transform.Position = 6, 1, 0
set: Sprite.Size = 0.6, 0.6
set: Sprite.Tint = #5F574F
deselect
create: Sprite
rename: Plank
set: Transform.Position = 8, 1, 0
set: Sprite.Size = 3, 0.4
set: Sprite.Tint = #AB5236

chapter: The rotate handle | Drag the knob to turn
look: 7, 1.5, 3.5
say: Here's a plank to put in the dungeon. Turning it used to mean typing an angle into the Inspector.
explain: handle:rotate | Rotate handle | Now the selection has a round handle sticking out of its top. Drag it around to turn.
rotate: Ctrl+30
expectvalue: Plank.Transform.Rotation.Z = 30
explain: field:Transform.Rotation | Snapped | Holding control snaps to fifteen degrees, so this is exactly thirty.
rotate: 20
explain: handle:rotate | Whole degrees | Without control it turns freely, but lands on whole degrees, so the Inspector keeps tidy numbers.
say: Each turn is one step to undo.
key: Ctrl+Z
expectvalue: Plank.Transform.Rotation.Z = 30

chapter: Turning several | Around the one picked last
select: Plank
select: Ctrl+Post
expectselected: Plank, Post
say: With several selected, the handle sits on the one picked last, here the post.
rotate: Ctrl+90
expectvalue: Post.Transform.Rotation.Z = 90
expectvalue: Plank.Transform.Rotation.Z = 120
expectat: Plank = 6, 3
explain: world:4.2, 4.8, 7.8, 0 | Swung around the post | Everything turns around it together. The plank swung up around the post like a gate, and both turned the same ninety degrees.
key: Ctrl+Z
expectat: Plank = 8, 1
say: And one undo puts them both back.
